Never select the i386 CRC assembly; crc32.c supplies the CRC and its table
on every arch.

unix/configure picks crc_i386.S (`-DASM_CRC`, CRCA_O=crc_gcc.o) when it finds
gas on i386/i686. That asm references `get_crc_table`, which the engine's
bitcode fold internalises (only the external asm uses it), so the i686 link
dies with `undefined symbol: get_crc_table`. The target cannot be singled out
(the engine builds i686 on an x86_64 host whose hostPlatform reports neither
i686 nor isLinux), and the C CRC is correct everywhere; on other arches the
crc_i386.S probe already fails, so this is a no-op there.

--- a/unix/configure
+++ b/unix/configure
@@ -156,8 +156,8 @@
   if test ! -s _crc_i386.s || grep error < _crc_i386.s > /dev/null; then
     :
   elif eval "$CC -c _crc_i386.s >/dev/null 2>/dev/null" && [ -f _crc_i386.o ]; then
-    CFLAGSR="${CFLAGSR} -DASM_CRC"
-    CRC32OA="crc_gcc.o"
+    :
+    CRC32OA=""
     echo "int foo() { return 0;}" > conftest.c
     $CC -c conftest.c >/dev/null 2>/dev/null
     echo Check if compiler generates underlines
